"$\\\",\\\"$L2a\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$2b\\\",null,{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Next.Metadata\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"$L2c\\\"}]}]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"meta\\\",null,{\\\"name\\\":\\\"next-size-adjust\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"\\\"}]]}]\\n14:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"link\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"rel\\\":\\\"stylesheet\\\",\\\"href\\\":\\\"/_next/static/chunks/2mc_yspokhq9v.css\\\",\\\"precedence\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"crossOrigin\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"nonce\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\"}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"2d:I[97367,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/38514q3x-5nzy.js\\\"],\\\"OutletBoundary\\\"]\\n11:C\\n17:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L2\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/about\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"About Us\\\"}]\\n18:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L2\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/contact\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Contact\\\"}]\\n19:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L2\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/privacy-policy\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Privacy Policy\\\"}]\\n1a:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L2\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/terms\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Terms\\\"}]\\n1b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-10 pt-7 border-t border-slate-800 flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4 justify-between items-center\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-xs text-slate-500 text-center md:text-left\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"© \\\",2026,\\\" Green Engineering Tools. All rights reserved.\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"max-w-2xl text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500 text-center md:text-right\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Engineering decision-support tools for EN 15804-aligned lifecycle analysis and LEED whole-building LCA workflows. Formal certification and compliance remain subject to project-specific requirements and independent review.\\\"}]]}]\\n1c:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"This calculator is built for construction material schedules rather than one-off household estimates. It can import CSV or BIM-derived quantities, reconcile unknown products, calculate lifecycle modules, compare baseline and proposed models, and normalize results by gross floor area.\\\"}]\\n1d:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",\\\"workflow\\\",{\\\"id\\\":\\\"workflow\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"scroll-mt-24\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"How to calculate embodied carbon from a material schedule\\\"}],\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"ol\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-5 space-y-3 list-decimal pl-6 text-slate-700 leading-7\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Export or prepare a schedule containing at least material name, quantity and unit.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Export or prepare a schedule containing at least material name, quantity and unit.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Upload the CSV and map its columns to material, quantity and unit fields.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Upload the CSV and map its columns to material, quantity and unit fields.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Review automatic material matches and resolve unknown names to appropriate EPD or other supported datasets.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Review automatic material matches and resolve unknown names to appropriate EPD or other supported datasets.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Check declared units and correct any conversion warnings before relying on the total.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Check declared units and correct any conversion warnings before relying on the total.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Enter project-specific transport distance and mode when A4 is required.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Enter project-specific transport distance and mode when A4 is required.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Set the building study period and review reference service life for products that may need replacement.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Set the building study period and review reference service life for products that may need replacement.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Review A-C results, Module D separately, and any missing-data warnings.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Review A-C results, Module D separately, and any missing-data warnings.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Normalize by gross floor area when comparing carbon intensity between design options.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Normalize by gross floor area when comparing carbon intensity between design options.\\\"}]]}],\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\"]}]\\n1e:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",\\\"formula\\\",{\\\"id\\\":\\\"formula\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"scroll-mt-24\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Simple A1-A3 calculation example\\\"}],[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Suppose a project contains 100 m³ of a material and the selected EPD reports A1-A3 GWP of 250 kg CO₂e per m³. If the declared quantity is 1 m³ and the units are compatible, the product-stage calculation is 100 × 250 = 25,000 kg CO₂e.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The arithmetic is simple; selecting the correct factor and unit is the difficult part. If the project quantity were in tonnes while the EPD were declared per cubic metre, a density would be required. Without a defensible density, the calculator should stop the conversion rather than return a confident but unsupported number.\\\"}]],\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-6 rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-5\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-black text-amber-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Use the example to understand the formula, not as a default carbon factor\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-2 leading-7 text-amber-900\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The 250 kg CO₂e/m³ value above is illustrative. Real projects should use an appropriate dataset for the product, geography, specification and declared unit.\\\"}]]}]]}]\\n1f:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",\\\"materials\\\",{\\\"id\\\":\\\"materials\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"scroll-mt-24\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Construction materials that can be evaluated\\\"}],[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The workflow is material-agnostic. Concrete, structural steel, reinforcement, timber, insulation, glazing, aluminium, gypsum products, finishes and assemblies can all be evaluated when the project quantity can be related to an appropriate environmental dataset.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"For early design, generic datasets may help compare broad options. For procurement, product-specific EPDs can provide more relevant manufacturer or supply-chain information. The source type should remain visible so users can distinguish early assumptions from later product selections.\\\"}]],\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\"]}]\\n20:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",\\\"intensity\\\",{\\\"id\\\":\\\"intensity\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"scroll-mt-24\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"How kg CO₂e/m² helps compare buildings\\\"}],[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"A total building result answers how much carbon is associated with the modeled scope. Carbon intensity answers how much impact is associated with each square metre of gross floor area. If the selected A-C result is 2,000,000 kg CO₂e and the building contains 10,000 m², the intensity is 200 kg CO₂e/m².\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Intensity is useful for benchmarking, but only when projects use comparable boundaries and assumptions. A structural-only study cannot be fairly compared with a study that includes structure, enclosure, interiors and site hardscape without adjusting the scope.\\\"}]],\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\"]}]\\n21:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",\\\"mistakes\\\",{\\\"id\\\":\\\"mistakes\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"scroll-mt-24\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Common mistakes in construction carbon calculations\\\"}],\\\"$undefined\\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"ul\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-5 space-y-3 list-disc pl-6 text-slate-700 leading-7\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Multiplying quantities by an EPD factor before checking the declared unit.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Multiplying quantities by an EPD factor before checking the declared unit.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Treating a missing EPD module as zero impact.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Treating a missing EPD module as zero impact.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Using a product-specific EPD for a materially different product or strength class.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Using a product-specific EPD for a materially different product or strength class.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Applying one transport distance and weight assumption to every material without review.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Applying one transport distance and weight assumption to every material without review.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Adding Module D directly into A-C without explaining the reporting convention.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Adding Module D directly into A-C without explaining the reporting convention.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Comparing buildings with different floor areas, functions or study periods as if they were equivalent.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Comparing buildings with different floor areas, functions or study periods as if they were equivalent.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"Reporting a precise total while a large percentage of the project remains unmapped.\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Reporting a precise total while a large percentage of the project remains unmapped.\\\"}]]}],\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\"]}]\\n22:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",\\\"when-use\\\",{\\\"id\\\":\\\"when-use\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"scroll-mt-24\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"When this online calculator is most useful\\\"}],[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The tool is particularly useful during option studies, design development, quantity takeoff review, material procurement and educational analysis. It gives teams a common place to connect quantities, environmental data and lifecycle assumptions.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"For formal submissions, treat the calculator as part of a documented professional workflow. Verify EPDs at the source, record project assumptions and use the rules of the applicable certification or reporting framework.\\\"}]],\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"$undefined\\\"]}]\\n23:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-16 border-t border-slate-200 pt-10\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-slate-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Frequently asked questions\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-6 space-y-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"Is this a free embodied carbon calculator for construction materials?\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"cursor-pointer list-none p-5 font-black text-slate-900 flex gap-4 justify-between\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Is this a free embodied carbon calculator for construction materials?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-emerald-600 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"+\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"px-5 pb-5 text-slate-700 leading-7\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Yes. The browser-based calculator is intended to let users import material quantities and calculate lifecycle carbon without a per-calculation fee. Connected data services may have their own access terms.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"Can I calculate embodied carbon from a CSV?\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"cursor-pointer list-none p-5 font-black text-slate-900 flex gap-4 justify-between\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Can I calculate embodied carbon from a CSV?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-emerald-600 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"+\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"px-5 pb-5 text-slate-700 leading-7\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Yes. Upload a CSV, map the material, quantity and unit columns, then resolve any unknown materials before reviewing the result.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"Can the calculator report kg CO₂e per m²?\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"cursor-pointer list-none p-5 font-black text-slate-900 flex gap-4 justify-between\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Can the calculator report kg CO₂e per m²?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-emerald-600 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"+\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"px-5 pb-5 text-slate-700 leading-7\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Yes. Enter gross floor area and the tool can normalize the selected building result to kg CO₂e/m².\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"Does an embodied carbon calculator replace an LCA professional?\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"cursor-pointer list-none p-5 font-black text-slate-900 flex gap-4 justify-between\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Does an embodied carbon calculator replace an LCA professional?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-emerald-600 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"+\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"px-5 pb-5 text-slate-700 leading-7\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"No. It can automate arithmetic and data handling, but project scope, functional equivalenc